\ wallet.fam — the wallet (docs/GUI_WALLET.md, phase 1), for wm's wallet
\ window: wm runs it as the session's user in the user's home, on pipes,
\ and it speaks the wallet's messages (docs/GUI_WALLET.md, The wallet's
\ messages): a JSON object a line each way, the first line wm's unlock
\ with the session's password, then each request answered by its op with
\ its id echoed.  It reads compact JSON (as JSON.stringify writes it).  It
\ ends when its input does.
\
\ Its records are a tree in the user's home, .wallet (mode 700), as
\ tabminer's wallet keeps an LMDB environment: "secret" the phrase's
\ entropy and its BIP39 seed, sealed under the password as tabminer seals
\ them (1, the rounds, a salt, a nonce, then ChaCha20-Poly1305 of the 80
\ bytes with the 33 before as associated data, the key the first 32
\ bytes of PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 of the password and "tabminer wallet" ||
\ salt); "address" the address counter (8 bytes; a new or restored
\ wallet's starts at a random 60-bit number: old addresses are never
\ used again, docs/PRIVACY.md); "scan" 1 while a restore waits for its
\ first scan.  The password is the session's: wm's, as typed at logging
\ in.
\
\ The node is its API on 127.0.0.1:3738, without the token (reads are
\ open).  The wallet's outputs are found by reading the whole unspent set
\ (/v1/outputs, a thousand a request) and checking each memo's tag: one
\ of this wallet's has its key derived and its commitment checked before
\ it is recorded; one once in the set and no longer there was spent.  The
\ set is read again whenever the tip moves (the node asked every 4 s
\ while no request comes), and the tip told (an event); a reorganization
\ needs nothing more.  Reading block by block can come later, when the
\ set is large.
\
\ Built so far (step 2 of 4): unlock, create, restore, phrase, receive,
\ overview, scan; the tip told.  The rest are refused as not yet built.
\ uses: crypto/sha512.fam crypto/sha256.fam crypto/bip39.fam crypto/chacha.fam crypto/keccak.fam crypto/dilithium.fam
\ uses: node/arith.fam node/poseidon2.fam node/difficulty.fam node/pow.fam node/state.fam node/xmss.fam node/xsign.fam node/wkeys.fam node/wslate.fam
\ memory: 4096
: ibuf variable ;  : icnt variable ;  : obuf variable ;  : opos variable ;
: idb variable ;  : opb variable ;  : unl variable ;  : jr variable ;
: lp variable ;  : le variable ;

\ jo ( s -- )  s added to the line being written, each ' a double quote
\ (fam's strings hold none); jraw ( s -- ) s as it is; jend the line
\ written, a newline after it.
: jo
opos @ swap
begin dup c@ ?dup while dup 27 lit = if drop 22 lit then 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat
drop opos ! ;
: jraw  opos @ swap scpy opos ! ;
: jend  A lit opos @ c!  1 lit obuf @ opos @ obuf @ - 1 lit + write drop  obuf @ opos ! ;

\ jfm ( a key -- flag )  key (' for a double quote) at a.
\ jfind ( line key -- a | 0 )  just past the first key in the line.
: jfm
begin dup c@ if over c@ over c@ dup 27 lit = if drop 22 lit then = else 0 lit then while
	1 lit + swap 1 lit + swap
repeat
nip c@ 0= ;
: jfind
0 lit jr !  swap
begin dup c@ jr @ 0= and while
	2dup swap jfm if dup 2 lit pick strlen + jr ! then
	1 lit +
repeat 2drop jr @ ;

\ getid ( line -- )  the request's id at idb as sent (up to a comma or a
\ brace), or null; getop ( line -- ) its op at opb (31 bytes at most), or
\ empty.
: getid
idb @ swap "'id':" jfind ?dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 2C lit <> over 7D lit <> and and while dup c@ 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat drop
else "null" scpy then
0 lit swap c! ;
: getop
opb @ swap "'op':'" jfind ?dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 22 lit <> and  2 lit pick opb @ - 1F lit u< and while
		dup c@ 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat drop
then
0 lit swap c! ;

\ jstr ( line key dst max -- flag )  the string after key (as "'words':'")
\ at dst, its escapes undone (\" \\ \/ \n \t \r \b \f, \u00XX), NUL-ended,
\ max - 1 bytes at most; whether the key was there and the string fit.
: jsd variable ;  : jsm variable ;  : jsok variable ;
: jhx  dup 3A lit u< if 30 lit - else 20 lit or 57 lit - then F lit and ;   \ ( c -- n )
: jsput  jsm @ 1 lit u> if jsd @ c!  jsd @ 1 lit + jsd !  jsm @ 1 lit - jsm ! else drop 0 lit jsok ! then ;
: jstr
jsm !  jsd !  jfind dup jsok !
dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 22 lit <> and while
		dup c@ 5C lit = if
			1 lit +  dup c@
			dup 6E lit = if drop A lit else dup 74 lit = if drop 9 lit else dup 72 lit = if drop D lit else
			dup 62 lit = if drop 8 lit else dup 66 lit = if drop C lit else
			dup 75 lit = if drop dup 3 lit + c@ jhx 4 lit lshift over 4 lit + c@ jhx or  swap 4 lit + swap then
			then then then then then
			jsput
		else dup c@ jsput then
		1 lit +
	repeat
	c@ 0= if 0 lit jsok ! then
else drop then
0 lit jsd @ c!  jsok @ 0= 0= ;

\ jok  an answer begun: its id, ok; jerr ( s -- ) an error answered.
: jok  "{'id':" jo idb @ jraw ",'ok':true" jo ;
: jerr  "{'id':" jo idb @ jraw ",'ok':false,'error':'" jo jo "'}" jo jend ;
: op?  opb @ swap streq ;                                    \ ( s -- flag )

\ ── The records ──

: wfd variable ;  : pw variable ;  : have variable ;  : rec variable ;  : plain variable ;  : wkey variable ;
: salt2 variable ;  : wphr variable ;  : wseed variable ;  : wtmp variable ;  : wcnt variable ;
: wpk variable ;  : wsk variable ;  : waddr variable ;  : wf1 variable ;  : wf2 variable ;
:M ROUNDS 4E20 lit ;                         \ the password's PBKDF2 rounds (fam's: about 1.4 s)

\ wrand ( dst n -- )  n bytes from /dev/random.
: wrf variable ;  : wrd variable ;  : wrn variable ;
: wrand
wrn !  wrd !  "/dev/random" 0 lit open wrf !
begin wrn @ while
	wrf @ wrd @ wrn @ read  dup 0 lit > if dup wrd @ + wrd !  wrn @ swap - wrn ! else drop then
repeat
wrf @ close drop ;
\ wopen ( create? -- flag )  the tree open (made, mode 700, if asked).
: wopen
wfd @ 0< 0= if drop -1 lit else
	".wallet" TREE 2 lit or rot if CREATE or then open dup wfd !
	0< 0= dup if ".wallet" 1C0 lit chmod drop then
then ;
\ wget ( key buf n -- vlen | <0 )  one record, read in a snapshot.
\ wbeg  the writer's transaction begun; wset ( key value n -- ) a record
\ in it; wend ( -- ok ) it committed, all its records or none.
: wgk variable ;  : wtx variable ;
: wget  wf2 !  wf1 !  wgk !  wfd @ 0 lit txbegin  dup wgk @ dup strlen wf1 @ wf2 @ txget  swap txabort drop ;
: wbeg  wfd @ 1 lit txbegin wtx ! ;
: wset  wf2 !  wf1 !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ dup strlen wf1 @ wf2 @ txput drop ;
: wend  wtx @ txcommit 0= ;

\ wkdf ( pw rec -- )  wkey (32 bytes) = PBKDF2 of the password with the
\ record's rounds and "tabminer wallet" || its salt (16 bytes at 5).
: wkr variable ;  : wkp variable ;
: wkdf
wkr !  wkp !
salt2 @ "tabminer wallet" scpy  wkr @ 5 lit + swap 10 lit bcopy
wkp @ dup strlen salt2 @ 1F lit wkr @ 1 lit + le@ wtmp @ 40 lit pbkdf512
wtmp @ wkey @ 20 lit bcopy ;
\ wseal  rec (129 bytes) = plain (the entropy, the seed) sealed under pw:
\ 1, the rounds, a salt (16), a nonce (12), the 96 sealed bytes.
: wseal
1 lit rec @ c!  ROUNDS rec @ 1 lit + wkle!  rec @ 5 lit + 10 lit wrand  rec @ 15 lit + C lit wrand
pw @ rec @ wkdf
wkey @ rec @ 15 lit + rec @ 21 lit plain @ 50 lit rec @ 21 lit + aeseal ;
\ wunseal ( pw -- flag )  plain from the record, if the password is its.
: wunseal
"secret" rec @ 100 lit wget 81 lit =  rec @ c@ 1 lit = and
dup if
	drop rec @ wkdf
	wkey @ rec @ 15 lit + rec @ 21 lit rec @ 21 lit + 50 lit plain @ aeopen
else nip then ;

\ The address: the Dilithium key of the address counter, its id in text.
: waok variable ;
: waddr!
waok @ 0= if
	wcnt @ wtmp @ wkidsd  wtmp @ wpk @ wsk @ dilkey  wpk @ wtmp @ wkid  wtmp @ waddr @ wkaddr
	1 lit waok !
then ;
\ wrcnt  a new counter: 60 random bits.
: wrcnt
wcnt @ 8 lit wrand
wcnt @ @ 4 lit rshift  wcnt @ 4 lit + @ 1C lit lshift or
wcnt @ 4 lit + @ 4 lit rshift  wcnt @ 4 lit + !  wcnt @ ! ;
\ wmake ( scan? -- ok )  a wallet made from plain: the tree, its records
\ in one transaction; the master.
: wmake
1 lit wopen if
	wrcnt  wseal  0 lit waok !
	wbeg
	"secret" rec @ 81 lit wset
	1 lit wtmp @ c!  "format" wtmp @ 1 lit wset
	"address" wcnt @ 8 lit wset
	if 1 lit wtmp @ c!  "scan" wtmp @ 1 lit wset then
	wend
	dup if plain @ 10 lit + wkmast  1 lit have ! then
else drop 0 lit then ;
\ wload  an opened wallet's records: the counter, the master.
: wload  "address" wcnt @ 8 lit wget drop  plain @ 10 lit + wkmast  1 lit have !  0 lit waok ! ;

\ ── The node: its API (docs/NODE.md, The API), on 127.0.0.1:3738 ──

: hbuf variable ;  : hreq variable ;  : hs variable ;  : hn variable ;  : hres variable ;  : hpath variable ;
:M HMAX 40000 lit ;
: wcrlf  D lit over c!  1 lit +  A lit over c!  1 lit + ;      \ ( a -- a' )
\ hbody  hres = the body of the answer in hbuf (after the blank line).
: hbody
hn @ 3 lit - 0 lit do
	hres @ 0= if
		hbuf @ i + c@ D lit =  hbuf @ i + 1 lit + c@ A lit = and  hbuf @ i + 2 lit + c@ D lit = and
		if hbuf @ i + 4 lit + hres ! then
	then
loop ;
\ hget ( path -- body | 0 )  a GET answered 200: its body, NUL-ended.
: hget
hpath !  0 lit hn !  0 lit hres !
2 lit socket hs !
hs @ 2 lit 7F000001 lit E9A lit net 0< 0= if
	hreq @ "GET " scpy hpath @ scpy " HTTP/1.0" scpy wcrlf wcrlf hreq @ -
	hs @ hreq @ rot write drop
	begin hs @ hbuf @ hn @ + HMAX 1 lit - hn @ - read  dup 0 lit > while hn @ + hn ! repeat drop
	0 lit hbuf @ hn @ + c!
	hn @ C lit u< 0= if hbuf @ 9 lit + "200" 3 lit wssame if hbody then then
then
hs @ close drop  hres @ ;

\ Numbers of 64 bits, as nlo and dhi.
: nlo variable ;  : nhi variable ;  : ndc variable ;  : nla variable ;  : nlb variable ;  : nca variable ;  : ncb variable ;
: nls variable ;  : nc1 variable ;  : nc2 variable ;  : nq0 variable ;  : nq1 variable ;  : nq2 variable ;  : nq3 variable ;
: ndn variable ;  : ntmp variable ;
\ d10+ ( d -- )  dlo:dhi times ten, plus d.
: d10+
ndc !
nlo @ 3 lit lshift nla !  nlo @ 1D lit rshift nca !
nlo @ 1 lit lshift nlb !  nlo @ 1F lit rshift ncb !
nla @ nlb @ + nls !  nls @ nla @ u< 1 lit and nc1 !
nls @ ndc @ + dup nls @ u< 1 lit and nc2 !  nlo !
nhi @ A lit * nca @ + ncb @ + nc1 @ + nc2 @ + nhi ! ;
\ jnum ( a -- a' )  the decimal digits at a into dlo:dhi; a' past them.
: jnum  0 lit nlo !  0 lit nhi !  begin dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< while dup c@ 30 lit - d10+ 1 lit + repeat ;
\ dq16 ( r limb -- r' q )  one 16-bit step of dividing by ten.
: dq16  swap 10 lit lshift or  dup A lit /  tuck A lit * -  swap ;
\ du10 ( -- r )  dlo:dhi divided by ten; the remainder.
: du10
0 lit  nhi @ 10 lit rshift dq16 nq3 !  nhi @ FFFF lit and dq16 nq2 !
nlo @ 10 lit rshift dq16 nq1 !  nlo @ FFFF lit and dq16 nq0 !
nq3 @ 10 lit lshift nq2 @ or nhi !  nq1 @ 10 lit lshift nq0 @ or nlo ! ;
\ ddig ( lo hi n -- )  its decimal digits at dtmp, least first, n at
\ least; how many in dn.
: ddig
ndc !  nhi !  nlo !  0 lit ndn !
begin du10 30 lit + ntmp @ ndn @ + c!  ndn @ 1 lit + ndn !  nlo @ nhi @ or 0= ndn @ ndc @ u< 0= and until ;
\ jc ( c -- )  a byte added to the line being written.
: jc  opos @ c!  opos @ 1 lit + opos ! ;
\ wamt ( lo hi -- )  an amount in coins, its ten decimals, written.
: wamt
B lit ddig
ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ jc  ndn @ 1 lit - i - A lit = if 2E lit jc then loop ;
\ wdec ( lo hi -- )  a number in decimal, written.
: wdec  1 lit ddig  ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ jc loop ;
\ dstr ( lo hi dst -- dst' )  the same into a string.
: dstr  -rot 1 lit ddig  ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ over c!  1 lit + loop  0 lit over c! ;
\ jhexb ( a dst n -- )  n bytes from 2n hex digits at a.
: jhexb  0 lit do over i 1 lit lshift + c@ jhx 4 lit lshift  2 lit pick i 1 lit lshift + 1 lit + c@ jhx or  over i + c! loop 2drop ;
\ ── The outputs: records "o" || commitment (33 bytes), 48 bytes each ──
\ +0 the nonce (4 canonical words), +10 the amount, +18 the position (8;
\ all ones: not yet in the set), +20 the height it was made at, +24 the
\ state (0 unspent, 1 reserved, 2 spent), +25 the first leaf, +26 leaves
\ used, +27 recovered (found by a scan, not made here: its leaves the
\ second half's, as tabminer's), +28 the scan that last saw it.

: okey variable ;  : orec variable ;  : wkl variable ;  : sgen variable ;
: ecom variable ;  : emem variable ;  : eamt variable ;  : epos variable ;  : eh variable ;  : ecb variable ;
: xk variable ;  : wxpk variable ;  : kseed variable ;  : scur variable ;  : scnt variable ;  : sfrom variable ;
: ltip variable ;  : lh variable ;  : nodeok variable ;  : okn variable ;  : ppath variable ;
\ wgetk ( key klen buf n -- vlen )  in the writer's transaction.
: wgetk  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txget ;
: wsetk  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txput drop ;
\ wone  one output of the set (ecom, emem, eamt, epos, eh) checked: a
\ known one's position and scan noted; an unknown one with this wallet's
\ tag, its key derived and its commitment checked, recorded as found.
: wone
79 lit okey @ c!  ecom @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk 30 lit = if
	epos @ orec @ 18 lit + 8 lit bcopy  eh @ @ orec @ 20 lit + !  sgen @ orec @ 28 lit + !
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
else
	emem @ wkopen if
		kseed @ wkkey  kseed @ 4 lit xk @ xkgen  xk @ wxpk @ xkpub
		wxpk @ eamt @ ecb @ wkcom  ecb @ ecb @ 20 lit + wkcan
		ecb @ 20 lit + ecom @ 20 lit wssame if
			orec @ 30 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
			emem @ orec @ 10 lit bcopy  eamt @ orec @ 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy  epos @ orec @ 18 lit + 8 lit bcopy
			eh @ @ orec @ 20 lit + !  wtmp @ 1 lit wrand  wtmp @ c@ 7 lit and orec @ 25 lit + c!
			1 lit orec @ 27 lit + c!  sgen @ orec @ 28 lit + !
			okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
		then
	then
then ;
\ wpage ( -- n )  a page of the set from sfrom (8 bytes) checked: how many.
: wpage
0 lit scnt !
ppath @ "/v1/outputs?from=" scpy  sfrom @ @ sfrom @ 4 lit + @ rot dstr "&count=1000" scpy drop
ppath @ hget dup scur !
if
	wbeg
	begin scur @ "'position':" jfind ?dup while
		jnum scur !  nlo @ epos @ !  nhi @ epos @ 4 lit + !
		scur @ "'commitment':'" jfind ecom @ 20 lit jhexb
		scur @ "'memo':'" jfind emem @ 14 lit jhexb
		scur @ "'amount':" jfind jnum drop  nlo @ eamt @ !  nhi @ eamt @ 4 lit + !
		scur @ "'height':" jfind jnum scur !  nlo @ eh @ !
		wone  scnt @ 1 lit + scnt !
		\ the next page from the position after this one
		epos @ @ 1 lit + dup sfrom @ !  0= if epos @ 4 lit + @ 1 lit + else epos @ 4 lit + @ then sfrom @ 4 lit + !
	repeat
	wend drop
then
scnt @ ;
\ wspent  the outputs once in the set and not seen by this scan: spent.
: wspent
wbeg
79 lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 79 lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <>  orec @ 28 lit + @ sgen @ <> and  orec @ 24 lit + c@ 2 lit <> and if
		2 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
	then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wend drop ;
\ wscan ( -- ok )  the whole unspent set read through the node.
: wscan
"gen" wtmp @ 4 lit wget 4 lit = if wtmp @ @ else 0 lit then 1 lit + sgen !
0 lit sfrom @ !  0 lit sfrom @ 4 lit + !  1 lit nodeok !
begin wpage dup 0= if hres @ 0= if 0 lit nodeok ! then then 3E8 lit u< until
nodeok @ if
	wspent
	wbeg  sgen @ wtmp @ !  "gen" wtmp @ 4 lit wset  0 lit wtmp @ c!  "scan" wtmp @ 1 lit wset  wend drop
then
nodeok @ ;
\ wtick  the node asked for its tip; when it moved, the set scanned again
\ and the tip told (an event).
: wtick
have @ if
	"/v1/status" hget ?dup if
		dup "'height':" jfind jnum drop nlo @ lh !
		"'tip':'" jfind wtmp @ 40 lit bcopy  0 lit wtmp @ 40 lit + c!
		wtmp @ ltip @ streq 0= if
			wscan if
				ltip @ wtmp @ scpy drop
				"{'event':'tip','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec ",'hash':'" jo ltip @ jraw "'}" jo jend
			then
		then
	else 0 lit nodeok ! then
then ;
\ wsum ( state pend acc -- )  the amounts of the outputs in a state added
\ up at acc (8 bytes): pend 0 those in the set, 1 those not yet, 2 both.
: sst variable ;  : sacc variable ;  : spend variable ;
: wsum
sacc !  spend !  sst !
0 lit sacc @ !  0 lit sacc @ 4 lit + !
wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
79 lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 79 lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	orec @ 24 lit + c@ sst @ =
	spend @ 2 lit =  orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit = 1 lit and spend @ = or  and if
		orec @ 10 lit + @ sacc @ @ + dup sacc @ @ u< 1 lit and  orec @ 14 lit + @ + sacc @ 4 lit + @ + sacc @ 4 lit + !  sacc @ !
	then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wtx @ txabort drop ;
: wsum.  dup @ swap 4 lit + @ wamt ;                      \ ( acc -- )  written

\ ── The requests ──

: tried variable ;
: nowal  "no wallet yet: create or restore one" jerr ;
: sa1 variable ;  : sa2 variable ;  : sa3 variable ;
: oview
wtick
0 lit 0 lit sa1 @ wsum  0 lit 1 lit sa2 @ wsum  1 lit 2 lit sa3 @ wsum
jok ",'confirmed':'" jo sa1 @ wsum.  "','pending':'" jo sa2 @ wsum.  "','unverified':'0.0000000000','reserved':'" jo sa3 @ wsum.
"','locked':'0.0000000000','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec  ",'node':'" jo nodeok @ if "synced" else "not reached" then jo "'}" jo jend ;
\ oscan  the whole set scanned again now; the tip and the scan told.
: oscan
have @ 0= if nowal else
	jok "}" jo jend
	0 lit ltip @ c!  wtick
	"{'event':'scan','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec ",'of':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec "}" jo jend
then ;
: ocreate
have @ if "there is a wallet already" jerr else
	plain @ 10 lit wrand  plain @ wphr @ b39phr  wphr @ "" plain @ 10 lit + b39seed drop
	0 lit wmake if jok ",'words':'" jo wphr @ jraw "'}" jo jend  wtick else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
then ;
: orestore
have @ if drop "there is a wallet already" jerr else
	dup "'words':'" wphr @ 100 lit jstr 0= if drop "no words" jerr else
		"'passphrase':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr drop
		wphr @ wtmp @ plain @ 10 lit + b39seed
		dup 0= if
			drop  wphr @ plain @ b39ent drop
			1 lit wmake if jok "}" jo jend  wtick else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
		else
			dup FFFFFFFF lit = if drop "a phrase is 12 words" jerr else
			FFFFFFFE lit = if "a word is not in the list" jerr else
			"the checksum of the words does not match: a word is wrong" jerr then then
		then
	then
then ;
: ophrase
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
	"'password':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr 0= if "no password" jerr else
		wtmp @ wunseal if
			plain @ wphr @ b39phr  jok ",'words':'" jo wphr @ jraw "'}" jo jend
		else "not the password" jerr then
	then
then ;
: oreceive
have @ 0= if nowal else waddr!  jok ",'address':'" jo waddr @ jraw "'}" jo jend then ;

\ unlk ( line -- )  the first line: wm's, the session's password.
: unlk
"unlock" op? if
	"'password':'" pw @ 100 lit jstr pw @ c@ 0= 0= and if
		0 lit wopen if
			"secret" rec @ 100 lit wget 0< if
				1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':false}" jo jend
			else
				pw @ wunseal if
					wload  1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':true}" jo jend  wtick
				else "{'op':'unlock','ok':false,'error':'the wallet is sealed under another password than the session'}" jo jend then
			then
		else 1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':false}" jo jend then
	else "{'op':'unlock','ok':false,'error':'no password'}" jo jend then
else drop "locked" jerr then ;

\ answer ( line -- )  a request answered by its op.
: answer
"overview" op? if drop have @ if oview else nowal then else
"receive" op? if drop oreceive else
"create" op? if drop ocreate else
"restore" op? if orestore else
"phrase" op? if ophrase else
"unlock" op? if drop "unlocked already" jerr else
"scan" op? if drop oscan else
"fees" op? "send" op? or "answer" op? or "finalize" op? or "activity" op? or
"cancel" op? or "bump" op? or if drop "not built yet" jerr else
drop "unknown op" jerr
then then then then then then then then ;

\ hline ( line -- )  a line read: only the first may unlock.
: hline
dup getid  dup getop
unl @ if answer else tried @ if drop "locked" jerr else 1 lit tried ! unlk then then ;

\ lines  each whole line read handled; the rest, a line begun, kept.
: lines
0 lit lp !
begin
	lp @ le !
	begin le @ icnt @ u<  ibuf @ le @ + c@ A lit <> and while le @ 1 lit + le ! repeat
	le @ icnt @ u<
while
	0 lit ibuf @ le @ + c!  ibuf @ lp @ + hline
	le @ 1 lit + lp !
repeat
icnt @ lp @ - dup if dup 0 lit do ibuf @ lp @ + i + c@ ibuf @ i + c! loop then
icnt ! ;

wsinit  b39load drop  xkinit
1004 lit alloc ibuf !  1000 lit alloc obuf !  1000 lit alloc idb !  20 lit alloc opb !
100 lit alloc pw !  100 lit alloc rec !  60 lit alloc plain !  20 lit alloc wkey !  40 lit alloc salt2 !
